From e15be90b6992f97e4100ee0aa65ea9dde0519300 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDR10+ vendor InfoFrame in a generic packet
 of its own

HDR10PLUS_VSIF (linux-9980) on amdgpu, for DCN, on HDMI and DisplayPort
connectors (not eDP).

DC sends the packet of the stream (dc_stream_state.hdr10plus_infopacket)
in a generic packet slot of its own, so that nothing else moves for it:
the vendor slot keeps the HDMI 1.4 vendor InfoFrame (the HDMI VIC of
2160p24, 25 and 30; 3D) or the Dolby VSIF of the tunnel, and the HDR
InfoFrame stays where it is.

- HDMI, DIO: generic packet 7, after the 0 to 5 of DCN 1 and the 0 to 6
  of DCN 2 and later;
- HDMI FRL, HPO: 13, after DSC (5 to 10), the HF-VSIF (11) and the
  VTEM (12);
- DisplayPort, DIO and HPO: 6, after the adaptive sync SDP (5); 4 is
  the immediate SDP and 7 the PPS of DSC. The HPO DisplayPort encoder
  gains the control register of its GSP 6 in its four register lists,
  and stops it with the others.

A change of HDR10PLUS_VSIF is a stream update of that packet
(hdr10plus_infopacket in dc_stream_update and dc_fast_update: an info
frame update of the fast type, as one of the vendor packet is), from
the commit that sets it: never a modeset. A stream that is created
takes it from the connector state. The atomic check refuses it with the
Dolby Vision tunnel, whose Dolby VSIF is the dynamic metadata of its
picture, and on a link that does not carry it.

Each encoder remembers whether it sends the HDR10+ packet
(hdr10plus_sent, which its stop functions clear), and its slot is
written only while HDR10+ is or was sent there: GSP6 on DisplayPort and
the HDMI packets 7 and 13 stay untouched otherwise, on eDP and on every
stream without HDR10+, as before this patch (what the DMUB firmware does
with them is not known).

Like every other DC packet, it is written when the commit is applied,
not latched with the flip: in which frame a change reaches the sink is
not verified.

Checked: W=1 without new warnings on the files changed and on the
resources that use the new register, the whole of drm compiled; host
test of the packet (amdgpu_dm_hdr10plus_packet()) with mutations. Not
run on a GPU.
